      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "impact_statement": "The trigger is the search list in /etc/resolv.conf or the LOCALDOMAIN environment variable. The image does not set LOCALDOMAIN, and /etc/resolv.conf is bind-mounted by the container runtime at start from the platform's DNS configuration, so only the platform operator controls it. Neither LLM API callers nor network peers can influence it. The worst-case impact under operator misconfiguration is a process abort (availability only)"
    }
